From: wosnxn123 <wosnxn123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Jul 2026 15:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix /tpr async chunk access on Folia/Canvas

RandomTeleport.getCenter called World.getHighestBlockYAt synchronously,
which throws "Cannot retrieve chunk asynchronously" on Folia/Canvas when
the command runs on a different world's region thread (e.g. player in
the nether running /tpr whose center is in the overworld). The center Y
is only used in the attemptRandomLocation fallback (the common path
already computes the final location Y async via getChunkAtAsync in
calculateRandomLocation), so use a placeholder Y in getCenter and
compute the real Y asynchronously in the fallback. Uses
World.getChunkAtAsync (the Folia-safe pattern introduced by 0005),
whose callback runs on the chunk's region thread where getHighestBlockYAt
is safe.

diff --git a/Essentials/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/RandomTeleport.java b/Essentials/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/RandomTeleport.java
--- a/Essentials/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/RandomTeleport.java
+++ b/Essentials/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/RandomTeleport.java
@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@

         final Location worldCenter = ess.getServer().getWorlds().get(0).getWorldBorder().getCenter();
-        worldCenter.setY(worldCenter.getWorld().getHighestBlockYAt(worldCenter) + HIGHEST_BLOCK_Y_OFFSET);
+        // Canvas/Folia: getHighestBlockYAt reads chunk synchronously and throws on cross-region access.
+        // Use a placeholder Y; the real Y is computed async in the attemptRandomLocation fallback.
+        worldCenter.setY(worldInfoProvider.getMaxHeight(worldCenter.getWorld()));
         setCenter(name, worldCenter);
         return worldCenter;
     }
@@ -184,3 +186,13 @@
         } else {
-            future.complete(center);
+            // Canvas/Folia: compute center Y async (chunk read must run on the chunk's region thread).
+            // Mirror calculateRandomLocation: nether uses getNetherYAt (getHighestBlockYAt returns
+            // the bedrock ceiling in the nether), other worlds use getHighestBlockYAt.
+            center.getWorld().getChunkAtAsync(center.getBlockX() >> 4, center.getBlockZ() >> 4).thenAccept(chunk -> {
+                if (World.Environment.NETHER.equals(center.getWorld().getEnvironment())) {
+                    center.setY(getNetherYAt(center));
+                } else {
+                    center.setY(center.getWorld().getHighestBlockYAt(center) + HIGHEST_BLOCK_Y_OFFSET);
+                }
+                future.complete(center);
+            });
         }
